## Asynchronous requests

Pass `async_req=True` to any API method (or to `ApiClient.call_api()`) to get back an `ApplyResult`; call `.get()` on it to obtain the result:

```python
thread = api_instance.get_account(account_id, async_req=True)
account = thread.get()
```

`async_req` replaces `async`, which is a reserved keyword since Python 3.7 and made the generated package fail to import. On Python 3.6 and older, `async=True` is still accepted as a deprecated alias, but it cannot be written in source code on Python 3.7+.

